1. Summary of the ProjectThe project focused on analyzing music track features to understand key audio characteristics—such as danceability, energy, tempo, and acousticness—and how they influence music recommendations. The core objective was to build a content-based recommendation model to suggest similar tracks based on user preferences, culminating in a structured performance report and visualization dashboard designed to assist in playlist curation.   2. Where the Dataset Came FromSource: The dataset was retrieved from Kaggle (specifically the bricevergnou/spotify-recommendation dataset).   Acquisition Tool: Ingested programmatically into the Python environment utilizing kagglehub.   3. The Tools UsedPython Environment & Libraries: Jupyter Notebooks running Python for data ingestion, cleaning, exploratory data analysis, and modeling.   KaggleHub: For sourcing and downloading the dataset.   Google Workspace (Google Docs & Sheets): For documenting scopes, building reports, and maintaining project tracking documentation.   4. Steps Taken to Analyze the DataData Acquisition & Ingestion: Set up the Python environment to pull the Spotify recommendation dataset via kagglehub.   Data Cleaning & Preprocessing: Addressed missing values, eliminated duplicate tracks, normalized numerical audio features, and formatted categorization variables.   Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA): Profiled the dataset to uncover distributions of audio features, correlation patterns, and unique genre-specific music characteristics.   Recommendation Modeling: Designed and evaluated a content-based recommendation algorithm utilizing cosine similarity on track audio features.   Performance Evaluation & Validation: Tested recommendation quality using sample track queries to evaluate feature importance in music similarity.   5. Findings and ResultsAudio Feature Dynamics: Found clear clusters and correlations among features like energy and danceability, which strongly influence how tracks group together musically.Model Effectiveness: The cosine similarity recommendation algorithm successfully identified and surfaced relevant similar tracks based purely on underlying quantitative audio traits rather than just metadata or genre labels.Deliverables Produced: Successfully established a cleaned, normalized dataset, a fully functional and well-commented Python recommendation script, and a comprehensive final analysis report.   6. Questions to Explore in the FutureHow would incorporating real-time user listening history or implicit feedback (skips, favorites) alter the recommendation weights?Can collaborative filtering techniques be layered on top of this content-based approach to improve personalization on live streaming platforms?How do contextual factors like time of day or seasonal trends impact user preference for specific audio features (e.g., acousticness vs. high energy)?
